---
description: Do not extract a one-use helper when inlining is shorter and clearer.
globs: '**/*.ts,**/*.tsx'
alwaysApply: true
---

Do not extract a helper that is called once if the body is clearer
inline and the extract adds more lines than it saves. This is especially
true of functions that only format or `console.info` a local object.

Keep an extracted function when it is reused, hides non-obvious logic, or
makes the caller substantially easier to read.

```typescript
// Avoid — called once and only wraps console.info
function printProcessingResults(result: ProcessResult): void {
  console.info(JSON.stringify(result, null, 2));
}
printProcessingResults({ elapsedMs, outputPath, processing });

// Prefer — inline when the helper is used once and adds no meaning
console.info(
  JSON.stringify({ elapsedMs, outputPath, processing }, null, 2)
);
```
